# Loop infrastructure — SELECTIVE tracking (2026-05-21 reform pivot).
#
# The reform session moved load-bearing loop behavior INTO .claude/ (agent
# prompts, helper scripts, slash command). Reproducibility — incident
# archeology for the 2026-05-19 permission-gate event, Tier-3 audit replays,
# prompt-bloat / Arbiter regressions — requires these to be tracked.
# Per-machine state (logs, cache, settings.local) stays ignored.
.claude/*

# Selectively un-ignore the load-bearing files
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/agents.references/
!.claude/scripts/
!.claude/commands/
!.claude/templates/
!.claude/workload_specs.yaml
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/SYSTEM_DESIGN.md
!.claude/REWRITE_SUMMARY.md
!.claude/TODO_deferred.md

# Inside the tracked dirs, re-ignore caches + transient
.claude/scripts/__pycache__/
.claude/scripts/tests/__pycache__/

# Per-machine / ephemeral / huge — explicitly ignored
.claude/projects/
.claude/logs/
.claude/cache/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/agents.v1.bak/

# Loop's scientific record lives at runs/_loop/ and is tracked by default
# (no entry needed — runs/ is not blanket-ignored, just specific subpaths).
# Lock files and per-machine scratch under _local/ are ignored:
runs/_loop/_local/

# Stray scratch notes occasionally dropped at repo root by tools / sessions.
# Real plans live in docs/design/ or docs/research_notes/.
/PLAN.md
/plan.md

# Simulation binary data (large, reproducible from config)
*.jld2

# Dashboard atlas cache (server-rebuildable from per-snap binaries)
runs/_dashboard_cache/

# Autopilot runtime sentinels (paused / dry_run / lock) — per-machine
# operational state, never source-of-truth.
runs/.autopilot.*

# Catalog human-layer (tags / index) — references local content_ids and
# is rebuildable; per-machine, not source-of-truth.
runs/.catalog/

# Per-run generated artefacts (movie frames, summaries, dashboard JSON)
runs/**/frames/
runs/**/summary.json
runs/**/dashboard_data.json
runs/**/movie.gif
runs/**/movie.mp4

# Auto-generated per-run output directories (`<inputbase>_<8 hex>/`).
# run_yaml copies the input YAML into the output dir, so config.yaml here
# is a duplicate of the tracked input under runs/<scan>/. Same for
# checkpoints and point_NNN.jld2 snapshots.
runs/*_[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f]/
# Variants with a trailing tag (e.g. `_pre_parserfix`) — same pattern,
# additional suffix after the hash.
runs/*_[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f]_*/
# CAS-keyed run dirs (Experiment / autopilot — 16 hex chars, no
# inputbase prefix). content_id(spec) is the basename.
runs/[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f]/
# Auto-saved copies that show up under docs/validation/ (mirrored runs).
docs/validation/**/*_[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f]/

# Generated dashboards (reproducible from data)
*.html

# Legacy output directory
**/output/
# Files generated by invoking Julia with --code-coverage
*.jl.cov
*.jl.*.cov

# Files generated by invoking Julia with --track-allocation. The plain
# `*.jl.mem` form covers the no-PID case; the second pattern catches the
# PID-suffixed dumps Julia writes when multiple julia processes run
# concurrently (e.g. `gpu_energy.jl.24028.mem`).
*.jl.mem
*.jl.[0-9]*.mem

# System-specific files and directories generated by the BinaryProvider and BinDeps packages
# They contain absolute paths specific to the host computer, and so should not be committed
deps/deps.jl
deps/build.log
deps/downloads/
deps/usr/
deps/src/

# Build artifacts for creating documentation generated by the Documenter package
docs/build/
docs/site/

# File generated by Pkg, the package manager, based on a corresponding Project.toml
# It records a fixed state of all packages used by the project. As such, it should not be
# committed for packages, but should be committed for applications that require a static
# environment.
Manifest*.toml
# ...but DO track the ROOT Manifest: this is an application (research codebase),
# not a registered library. A pinned Manifest makes CI reproducible and — the
# load-bearing reason here — stabilises the julia-actions/cache key so the
# 127-dependency precompile is restored instead of rebuilt (~3-5 min) every run.
# Regenerate with `julia --project=. -e 'using Pkg; Pkg.resolve()'` after dep
# changes. Sub-environment Manifests (test/, docs/, …) stay ignored.
!/Manifest.toml

# File generated by the Preferences package to store local preferences
LocalPreferences.toml
JuliaLocalPreferences.toml

# Perf-Ralph transient bench output (baseline.json is pinned, results.json
# is regenerated per loop iteration).
bench/results.json

# Runtime logs — transient stdout dumps from batch drivers, dashboards,
# perf-Ralph loops, etc. Scripts that need it `mkdir -p logs/...` on demand.
logs/
runs/**/_live_status.json
runs/eu151_edh/result_postfix_gs_32cube.jld2

# Sprint research output — transient log dumps + dry-run artifacts from
# scout / sweep / smoke scripts. Reproducible from the scripts in
# `scripts/sprint*_*.jl`; the durable record lives in commit messages and
# memory entries, not these working files.
runs/sprint*_*.txt
runs/sprint*_*.log
runs/sprint*_*/
runs/_dryrun_*/
runs/sysimage_build_log.txt
scripts/_*.txt

# Generated paper LaTeX/PDF (use scripts/manuscript/build_paper_latex.sh to regenerate)
docs/manuscript/papers/*/build/

# Tailscale TLS certs (per-machine, never commit)
dashboard/anko-wsl.*.crt
dashboard/anko-wsl.*.key

# Windows NTFS Alternate Data Streams ("Zone.Identifier") that get
# attached when files are downloaded on Windows / WSL. Not real
# content; always ignore.
*:Zone.Identifier


# Autopilot runtime state
runs/budget.toml
runs/.autopilot.lock
runs/.autopilot.paused
runs/.autopilot.metrics.jsonl
runs/.autopilot.errors.log

# Harness output (regenerated by test/test_reference_rhs.jl per run)
verify_outputs/

# Loop Engineering runtime sentinels (tick/done counters)
.loop/

# ── Per-run research outputs (2026-07-23 cleanup) ──────────────────────
# EdH / flower-protocol runs drop figures, movies, tomography data, notes and
# logs under runs/**/. These are reproducible from the tracked *.yaml configs,
# so ignore the generated artefacts but keep configs / scripts / *.md notes.
# NOTE: *.png is deliberately NOT ignored — figures are the deliverable and
# the rule above keeps them; only regenerable data/logs are dropped.
runs/**/*.mp4
runs/**/*.gif
runs/**/*.h5
runs/**/*.csv
runs/**/*.log
runs/**/*.json
runs/**/*.pdf
runs/**/*.aux
runs/**/*.txt

# macOS Finder metadata + Python bytecode caches (never source-of-truth)
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
# Local personal document — submitted thesis PDF, not part of the codebase
/修士論文_後藤_提出版.pdf
# LaTeX build artifacts (the .tex sources are tracked, the build products are not)
*.out
*.aux
*.toc
# result CSVs are regenerable (extract from jld2); keep figures (png), not data
runs/**/*.csv

# figure data lives on TSUBAME (runs/eu_shape_optimization/data/); repo keeps figures+code
docs/guides/figures/*.csv
docs/guides/figures/__pycache__/

# figs/ raw trajectory data archived on TSUBAME (runs/eu_evaporation_optimization/data/); repo keeps result PNGs + summaries
figs/**/*.csv

# phase-gap bench cell cache (see bench/phase_gap_report.jl)
.gap_cache/

# Mutation-harness output (test/mutation/run.jl)
mutation_out/
